    "explanation_of_the_difference": "Measured: over all 720 azimuths of all five sites the stored masks differ from the double-precision recomputation by up to 0.00 deg at 0 m and 0.00 deg at 2 m; when the recomputation rounds the terrain radius to single precision the largest difference falls to 0.3578 deg. Cause: in lunarnav/terrain.py, mask_from_grids evaluates 'MOON_RADIUS_M + heights' on a float32 array, so the terrain radius is rounded to 0.125 m (the float32 spacing at 1.74e6 m) while the observer radius stays in double precision. A height error of up to 0.0625 m is 0.36 deg for terrain 10 m away, 0.036 deg at 100 m and 0.004 deg at 1 km, so it matters where the horizon is the ground next to the observer (0 m masks). Effect on the 18.6-year Sun percentage (disk fraction): at most 0.0 points at 0 m and 0.0 points at 2 m.",
